# WN22-00-000170: Windows Server 2022 default permissions for the HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE registry hive must be maintained.
# Source: Windows Server 2022 STIG r8
# Severity: medium
# Generated from 01-extract/output/windows-server-2022-stig-r8-controls.json

META
    esp_id `win2022-wn22-00-000170-001`
    version `1.0.0`
    dsl_schema_version `1.0.0`
    platform `windows`
    criticality `high`

    title `Windows Server 2022 default permissions for the HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE registry hive must be maintained.`
    description `The registry is integral to the function, security, and stability of the Windows system. Changing the system's registry permissions allows the possibility of unauthorized and anonymous modification to the operating system.`
    author `scanset-security`
    tags `windows,server-2022,stig,medium,registry-acl,ntfs,ksi-iam-jit`

    control_mapping `KSI:KSI-IAM-JIT,NIST-800-53:AC-6(10)`
    control_objective `KSI-IAM-JIT`

    assessment_method `TEST`
    implementation_status `implemented`
    responsible_role `system-admin`

    control_origination `sp-system`
    inherited_from `Windows:server-2022:endpoint`
    customer_responsibility `configuration`

    remediation_days `30`
    recommendation `Maintain the default permissions for the HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE registry hive. The default permissions of the higher-level keys are noted below. HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SECURITY Type - "Allow" for all Inherited from - "None" for all Principal - Access - Applies to SYSTEM - Full Control - This key and subkeys Administrators - Special - This key and subkeys HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SOFTWARE Type - "Allow" for all Inherited from - "None" for all Principal - Access - Applies to Users - Read - This key and subkeys `

    component_id `comp-windows-registry-acl`

    impl_KSI_IAM_JIT `Windows Server implements KSI-IAM-JIT by asserting that the ACL on each registry key in the rule does not grant any nonprivileged principal greater-than-Read access, via Get-Acl through the windows_registry_acl CTN. The ESP scanner queries the policy via the windows_security_policy CTN and fails the policy if the value does not match the STIG-required state. Remediation sets the policy via secedit or Group Policy.`
    impl_AC_6_10 `Windows Server implements AC-6(10) by asserting that the ACL on each registry key in the rule does not grant any nonprivileged principal greater-than-Read access, via Get-Acl through the windows_registry_acl CTN. The ESP scanner queries the policy via the windows_security_policy CTN and fails the policy if the value does not match the STIG-required state. Remediation sets the policy via secedit or Group Policy.`

META_END

DEF
    OBJECT key_1
        key_path `HKLM:\SECURITY`
    OBJECT_END

    OBJECT key_2
        key_path `HKLM:\SOFTWARE`
    OBJECT_END

    OBJECT key_3
        key_path `HKLM:\SYSTEM`
    OBJECT_END

    STATE key_1_exists
        exists boolean = true
    STATE_END

    STATE key_1_fid_1
        allow_identities string not_contains `Users`
    STATE_END

    STATE key_1_fid_2
        allow_identities string not_contains `Everyone`
    STATE_END

    STATE key_1_fid_3
        allow_identities string not_contains `Anonymous`
    STATE_END

    STATE key_1_fid_4
        allow_identities string not_contains `Guest`
    STATE_END

    STATE key_1_fid_5
        allow_identities string not_contains `INTERACTIVE`
    STATE_END

    STATE key_1_fid_6
        allow_identities string not_contains `Authenticated`
    STATE_END

    STATE key_2_exists
        exists boolean = true
    STATE_END

    STATE key_2_face_1
        aces string not_contains `Everyone|Allow|FullControl`
    STATE_END

    STATE key_2_face_2
        aces string not_contains `Everyone|Allow|WriteKey`
